# 📌 Quick Notes / Cheat Sheet

| Concept    | Meaning                         | Example              |
| ---------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| Variable   | Name referring to a value       | `age = 25`           |
| Identifier | Name used to identify something | `age`, `calculate()` |
| Keyword    | Reserved Python word            | `if`, `for`, `def`   |
| Constant   | Value intended not to change    | `PI = 3.14`          |
| `input()`  | Takes input from user           | `name = input()`     |
| `int()`    | Converts to integer             | `int("25")`          |
| `float()`  | Converts to float               | `float("5.5")`       |
| `type()`   | Tells object's type             | `type(age)`          |

